NetSuite Requirements
Based on the NetSuite Adapter documentation and SAP community guidance:

NetSuite Token-Based Authentication (TBA) enabled (mandatory). [community.sap.com]
Roles & Permissions configured for integration (API role).
SuiteTalk Web Services (SOAP) or REST APIs enabled.
SuiteScript (RESTlet) enabled if using custom REST endpoints.
Support for multiple API versions — adapter allows selecting API version. [api.sap.com]
Custom records/fields documented if your environment has customizations.
Integration user created with API-only access.

1.2 SAP Requirements
From SAP Integration Suite and adapter documents:

SAP Integration Suite subscription (Standard or higher). [api.sap.com]
Cloud Integration capability enabled.
NetSuite Adapter for SAP Integration Suite installed (Cloud Foundry). [api.sap.com]
SAP credentials & API access depending on SAP product:

SAP ECC → BAPI / IDoc / RFC
SAP S/4HANA → OData APIs
SAP Business One → Service Layer APIs


Connectivity setup (proxy, firewall rules, OAuth tokens, certificates).

1.3 Infrastructure Requirements

Secure connection (HTTPS/TLS).
Firewall allowlisting for SAP → NetSuite endpoints.
For on‑prem SAP systems, SAP Cloud Connector may be required.
If using ETL middleware (Jitterbit, Celigo, Boomi, KingswaySoft), install their agents.

